+      <p class="eyebrow">Effective 27 October 2026</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
+      <div class="legal-summary"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><p><strong>No account, advertising, analytics or tracking.</strong> Your route library stays on your device. The included overview and place search work offline. Additional map downloads use Apple services; optional alternative map sources have separate technical and security processing.</p></div>
       <section><h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>Matthew Bilella, trading as Bilella Works in the United Kingdom, is responsible for personal information described in this policy. This is the data controller for support messages and information processed through this website. Contact <a href="mailto:bilellaworks@gmail.com">bilellaworks@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
-      <section><h2>What this policy covers</h2><p>This policy covers the current Ridge development build, its support service and this privacy page. The app is not yet available in the App Store, and this policy will be reviewed before release.</p></section>
-      <section><h2>Information stored on your device</h2><p>Ridge stores routes, waypoints, route geometry, route names, app preferences and downloaded map and terrain data locally on your device. This information provides the route library, editing, offline mapping and rehearsal features. Bilella Works cannot see or retrieve locally stored routes.</p></section>
-      <section><h2>Place search and online maps</h2><p>When you search for a place, the app uses Apple MapKit. Apple may process the search text, geographic context, IP address and technical request information needed to return results. The online overview map is also provided through Apple services. Bilella Works does not receive your place searches or Apple map activity.</p><p>The current build does not request access to your device's precise location. You choose a place, enter coordinates or tap the map to select a route start.</p></section>
-      <section><h2>Map downloads</h2><p>Ridge connects to the mapping catalogue configured in the app when you refresh available maps or request a download. The mapping server receives the technical request information needed to respond, which can include an IP address, request time, requested file, browser or app headers, and security logs. Ridge does not upload your saved routes or imported GPX files to the mapping server.</p><p>The current development build is configured for a local mapping server by default. If a different server address is configured, that server's operator controls its own logs and privacy practices.</p></section>
+      <section><h2>What this policy covers</h2><p>This policy covers Ridge for iPhone and iPad, its optional support service and this privacy page. TestFlight testing also uses Apple’s separate beta-testing services and privacy terms.</p></section>
+      <section><h2>Information stored on your device</h2><p>Ridge stores routes, waypoints, route geometry, names, notes, walking plans, checklist items, app preferences and downloaded map and terrain data locally on your device. This information provides the route library, editing, offline mapping and rehearsal features. Bilella Works cannot see or retrieve locally stored routes.</p></section>
+      <section><h2>Place search, maps and location</h2><p>The included UK overview and place-name search use data stored in the app or in saved map areas. Ridge does not send your search text or route geometry to Bilella Works to render the map or calculate a route.</p><p>A supported map view can request your location when you choose to show your position. Permission is optional and controlled in iOS Settings. This position is processed on your device for that view; Ridge does not upload it to Bilella Works or track your location in the background.</p></section>
+      <section><h2>Apple map downloads</h2><p>Apple downloads is the default map source. When you request additional terrain, Ridge uses Apple’s Background Assets system and Apple-hosted asset packs. Apple processes the account, network and technical information needed to deliver those files under its own terms and privacy policy. The request identifies the map pack needed for the area you selected; Ridge does not send Apple your saved route document, notes or checklist as part of this process.</p><p>Downloaded terrain is read locally while browsing, planning and previewing. Device and iCloud backups are controlled by Apple and your settings. Downloaded map caches are excluded from app backup where supported, and can be downloaded again.</p></section>
+      <section><h2>Alternative map sources and security</h2><p>You can explicitly choose a local or other compatible map server or a download link. That server receives the requested file, IP address, request time and technical headers needed to provide the download; its operator controls any logs. Use a server you trust. Ridge does not upload your route library or imported GPX files to a mapping server.</p><p>The retained Bilella Works protected download service, when used as an alternative source, verifies genuine app installations using Apple App Attest. It receives a device-level verification key identifier and cryptographic proofs, stores the verification public key and replay counter, and keeps per-device request and byte counters to enforce download allowances and prevent abuse. Short-lived authorisation records include the requested file path and byte range. This security information is not used for advertising, cross-app tracking or behavioural analytics, and is not linked to a Ridge account.</p><p>Short-lived authorisations expire after two minutes and are removed during later service requests. Device registrations and per-device usage counters in that retained service currently have no automatic expiry and remain until removed by the operator or the service is retired. Contact support about information held by that service. Normal Apple-hosted downloads do not require this alternative verification service.</p></section>
       <section><h2>GPX import and export</h2><p>You can choose to import a GPX file through Apple's document picker or export a confirmed route through the system share sheet. The app accesses a selected file only to perform the import or export you request. Once you save or share an exported file with another app, storage provider or person, their privacy practices apply to that copy.</p></section>
       <section><h2>Deleting information from the app</h2><p>You can delete an individual route from the Saved Routes list. This removes the local route document but does not remove downloaded maps. Deleting Ridge removes its remaining local routes, settings and downloaded app data from the device, subject to Apple's device and backup behaviour. Previously exported files must be deleted from wherever you saved them.</p></section>
       <section><h2>Advertising, analytics and tracking</h2><p>The current build contains no account system, advertising, tracking technology, crash-reporting SDK or third-party analytics SDK. It does not sell or share route data for advertising.</p></section>
       <section><h2>If you contact support</h2><p>Support is optional. If you email support, Bilella Works receives your email address, any name shown by your email service, your message and any device, operating-system or app details you choose to include. Ridge does not automatically attach routes, GPX files or diagnostics to an email.</p><p>We use this information to answer your request, investigate faults, protect the app and its users, and meet legal obligations. If you do not provide an email address and enough information about the issue, we may not be able to reply or investigate it.</p></section>
       <section><h2>Our lawful bases</h2><p>We use legitimate interests to answer support requests, fix faults and protect the security of the app and service. Those interests are providing effective support and maintaining a safe, reliable product. We use legal obligation where information must be kept or disclosed to comply with the law. We do not use support information for advertising or marketing.</p></section>
       <section><h2>How long support information is kept</h2><p>Normal support correspondence is deleted from the support mailbox within 12 months after the last contact. We may keep relevant information for longer while a security incident, complaint, legal claim or legal obligation remains active. It is deleted when that reason ends. Provider backups may take a short additional period to expire under the provider's retention process.</p></section>
-      <section><h2>Service providers and disclosures</h2><p>Apple provides place search, online maps, document selection, sharing, operating-system services and device backups. Optional support email is handled using Gmail by Google. This website is delivered and protected using Cloudflare. A configured mapping server supplies map and terrain downloads. These providers may process limited personal information needed to provide their services under their own privacy terms and security measures.</p><p>We may disclose information to professional advisers or public authorities only when reasonably necessary to establish or defend legal rights, prevent harm, or comply with the law. We do not sell personal information or share it for advertising.</p><p>Read <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>, the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.</p></section>
+      <section><h2>Service providers and disclosures</h2><p>Apple provides app and asset-pack distribution, optional location permission, document selection, sharing, operating-system services and device backups. Optional support email is handled using Gmail by Google. This website is delivered and protected using Cloudflare. A configured mapping server supplies map and terrain downloads. These providers may process limited personal information needed to provide their services under their own privacy terms and security measures.</p><p>We may disclose information to professional advisers or public authorities only when reasonably necessary to establish or defend legal rights, prevent harm, or comply with the law. We do not sell personal information or share it for advertising.</p><p>Read <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>, the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.</p></section>
       <section><h2>This website</h2><p>Bilella Works does not use visitor accounts, advertising, marketing pixels or visitor analytics on this website. When you visit, Cloudflare necessarily receives technical request information such as your IP address, requested page, browser headers, time of request and security signals so it can deliver and protect the site. Bilella Works does not combine this information with app data or use it to profile visitors.</p><p>The lawful basis for this processing is legitimate interests in operating a secure and reliable website. Cloudflare controls its own retention of network and security records under its terms and privacy policy.</p></section>
       <section><h2>International processing</h2><p>Apple, Google and Cloudflare operate internationally, so support, map or website information may be processed outside the United Kingdom. Where UK law treats a transfer controlled by Bilella Works as restricted, we use an applicable UK adequacy regulation or another safeguard permitted by UK data protection law.</p></section>
       <section><h2>Your privacy rights</h2><p>Depending on the circumstances, you may ask for access to personal information, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or object to processing based on legitimate interests. Email <a href="mailto:bilellaworks@gmail.com">bilellaworks@gmail.com</a> to make a request. We may ask for enough information to verify your identity. These rights apply to support or website information held by Bilella Works. Bilella Works cannot access routes stored only on your device or information controlled separately by Apple or another mapping server.</p><p>You can also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office. Visit the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ICO complaint page</a> for current contact options.</p></section>
