+          <details><summary>How do I start a route?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>In Explore, zoom into saved terrain to enter 3D, then choose Plan your route and add points. Download an area first if the map shows that its terrain is not saved. Routes are saved locally; Finish editing keeps the route available to edit, preview or export.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>Do I need to download the whole UK?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. The app includes the UK overview and a Snowdon demonstration. Select the area you need and review its size before confirming the download. Allow free device storage for the download and its offline copy, and check it opens before leaving.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>A map area will not download<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Choose Apple downloads in Ridge Settings, use a reliable connection and check free storage. For a TestFlight build, use the Apple Account invited to that test. Follow any retry or resume action in the area card. Keep the existing app installed while investigating; deleting it can remove your locally saved routes.</p><p>If the download still fails, email support with the area name, exact error, app version and iOS version. Do not include a private route unless you choose to share it.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>What works without an internet connection?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The included overview and place-name search work offline. Saved map areas support 3D exploration, route planning and preview. Download additional terrain before you go, and test reopening it in airplane mode.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>How do I preview or edit a saved route?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Open Routes and choose a route, then use Edit or Preview route. Its terrain must be saved to open it in 3D. During preview you can pause and scrub through the route using its progress controls or elevation plot.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>Where are pace, finish time and the packing checklist?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Open a route’s menu and choose Before you go. Adjust walking pace, breaks and an optional departure time; review route legs, saved-map coverage, notes and checklist items. These planning estimates do not change flight speed and cannot account for every ground or weather condition.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>How do I import or export GPX?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Choose Import GPX from Routes to select a file. To export, open a route’s menu and choose Export GPX. Separate GPX track sections remain separate. Walking plans and packing checklists stay in Ridge and are not part of the GPX file.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>Is Ridge free?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The current features are free during early access. Pricing may change in future versions. Feedback is welcome and optional; it is not a condition of using the app.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>Does Ridge guide me while I walk?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Ridge is a route-planning and terrain-preview tool. It does not provide live turn-by-turn navigation. Check current weather, access, route suitability and your equipment before setting out.</p></details>
+          <details><summary>Does Ridge collect my route data?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>There is no Ridge account, advertising or behavioural analytics. Your route library stays on your device. Apple handles the default additional map downloads; optional alternative sources have their own technical and security processing. Read the <a href="/apps/ridge/privacy/">Ridge privacy policy</a> for details.</p></details>
